  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Humanitarian Response in Northern Chile: Provision of Shelter and Food to Migrant Families in Iquique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2020, and in the context of border closures due to the COVID-19 pandemic, irregular migratory flows into Chile began to increase exponentially, fostering a humanitarian crisis in the north of the country. In the present-day, considerable inflows of irregular migrants persist throughout the northern regions along border zones characterized by adverse weather conditions and inadequate infrastructure. In response to the need for protection for those who continue to enter Chile, this project, provides continuity and complements current efforts by other United Nations agencies, the Government of Chile, and Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) in the national territory by means of implementing temporary shelter and food to migrant families in Iquique located in the Tarapac&#xe1; Region.</narrative>
  </description>
